# Folded pipelines' stores streamed (foldsim-fold-static fold-store-stream; the
# constant-shell fold's fold stores, audit item C): every store of a depth of 2
# or more is a virtual memory in HBM, whatever its size and the state scratch,
# and its on-chip side is fixed: a landing ring of L entries (the schedule's,
# not the instance count's) holds each issue's {instance, rows, enables} and
# results, and the L-th state pass after the issue sends its write with the
# instance's read of the row its next pass reads; with vmem-rings the answers
# go to the class's ring (an image row per instance in HBM, prefetched a lead
# ahead), so no buffer has an entry per instance. Driver/Inputs/fold_stream:
# sixteen leaves, stores of 48 bits (1-bit pipeline), 512 and 384 bits (8-bit
# ones) and 38,400 bits (600 bits wide), against models of the kernel's
# controllers (Inputs/tb_vmem_multi.sv; the ring's image with its tag bits):
# responses 1 to 60 host cycles late, stalled channels, controllers out of
# room, two copies with bubbles. A class whose passes leave no such L (passes
# too close, or a few instances: Driver/Inputs/fold_hbm) keeps a landing entry
# per instance, the reads at the passes, as fold-store-hbm.
# REQUIRES: verilator
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/fold_stream
# Packed passes (II 22): a ring of 8 entries; the read buffers per instance.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/all --static --fold-store-stream Leaf > %t/all.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ALL < %t/all.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR < %t/all/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/vmem_bind.py %t/all/foldsim_sim.json %t/all
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -I%t/all --top-module tb -Mdir %t/all/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_multi.sv top.sv %t/all/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/all/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/all/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAST
# RUN: %t/all/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/all/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# Spread passes (state in RAM, II 67) and vmem rings: rings of 2 entries, no
# entry per instance anywhere.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ring --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --fold-store-stream --vmem-rings 4 Leaf > %t/ring.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RING < %t/ring.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RIR < %t/ring/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/vmem_bind.py %t/ring/foldsim_sim.json %t/ring
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -I%t/ring --top-module tb -Mdir %t/ring/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_multi.sv top.sv %t/ring/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/ring/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/ring/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/ring/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+5 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/ring/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+6 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# fold-store-rings without vmem-rings: the stores' read buffers alone as rings
# (the same II, no read buffer row and no pending bit per instance).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/fr --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --fold-store-stream --fold-store-rings 4 Leaf > %t/fr.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FR < %t/fr.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FRIR < %t/fr/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/vmem_bind.py %t/fr/foldsim_sim.json %t/fr
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique -I%t/fr --top-module tb -Mdir %t/fr/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_multi.sv top.sv %t/fr/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/fr/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/fr/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+11 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/fr/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+12 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/fr/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+13 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# Without it (the same command): a pending bit per instance a store.
